cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or refer to Deep32, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Deep32: Evidence-first question answering for network and security engineering"
abstract: >-
  Deep32 answers network and security engineering questions from a local, versioned corpus of RFCs and vendor
  documentation. A language-model agent is given evidence tools over the Model Context Protocol and a fixed
  protocol: resolve every identifier, read whole sections, check the standing of every RFC cited, and verify
  every quotation against the source text before answering.
authors:
  - family-names: Cummings
    given-names: Jeffrey A.
    email: jacummings@acm.org
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-8091-4637"
repository-code: "https://github.com/hellobpdu/deep32"
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - network engineering
  - network security
  - Model Context Protocol
  - RFC
  - verification
